# GG2: AGENT TURNS and HIT MID-COLD, arm B (A = c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix; B = c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-traffic), as ONE prefix job of two plans. Eight coding agents of eight turns, 192-token answers (agent-turns-prefix), then a salted hit turn that arrives while an unsalted cold 254k
# prompt is in prefill beside six decoding seats (levern-hit). TIMED: no audits, no digests. READ: G pass = p90 turn latency B <= A and p50 B <= 1.05 x A, reuse engaged (Q > 0), transcripts equal; G kill = p90 B > 1.10 x A
# (the cutover rests on THIS pair; the second pair is a later window); GH pass = the hit's TTFT during the cold arrival at most its solo plus 1.5 s on B (a run whose hit arrived in a 16,384-token step is INCONCLUSIVE, never FAIL).
# The box clips every arm's docker timeout (--box-seconds). ARC runners at zero. Measured basis: an agent-turns arm took 16.5 minutes (v580).
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the W-2 window pack (tp4-w2-levern-jobs: Lever N robustness, then the cutover; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/stage1-windows and push the job's tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Names no rig, card, host or registry. ORDER.txt has the order,
# the classes, the minutes, the boxes, the tags and every rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11 is the window image (the combined branch's engine with the Lever N traffic profile baked in as its
# default); a job that names tp4-serve-10 runs the production base image. C2_BOX_MINUTES is the job's box: the workflow enforces it from inside, it never cancels a run.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11b
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=agent-turns-prefix,levern-hit
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-traffic
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
C2_PREFIX_AGENTS=8
C2_BOX_MINUTES=55
